[1660.61735, "o", "3:MTEB is a benchmark for evaluating the quality of embeddings in various tasks. It supports the following commands:\r\n5:- mteb run: Runs a model on a set of tasks\r\n6:- mteb available_tasks: Lists the available tasks within MTEB\r\n7:- mteb create_meta: Creates the metadata for a model card from a folder of results\r\n11:To run a model on a set of tasks, use the `mteb run` command. For example:\r\n14:mteb run -m average_word_embeddings_komninos \\\r\n16:         --output_folder mteb_output \\\r\n20:This will create a folder `mteb_output/{model_name}/{model_revision}` containing the results of the model on the specified tasks supplied as a json\r\n21:file: \"{task_name}.json\".\r\n26:To list the available tasks within MTEB, use the `mteb available_tasks` command. For example:\r\n29:mteb available_tasks # list all available tasks\r\n30:mteb available_tasks --task_types Clustering # list tasks of type Clustering\r\n44:Once a model is run you can create the metadata for a model card from a folder of results, use the `mteb create_meta` co"]
[1660.61741, "o", "mmand. For example:\r\n47:mteb create_meta --results_folder mteb_output/average_word_embeddings_komninos/{revision} \\\r\n48:                 --output_path model_card.md\r\n51:This will create a model card at `model_card.md` containing the metadata for the model on MTEB within the YAML frontmatter. This will make the model\r\n54:An example frontmatter for a model card is shown below:\r\n60:model-index:\r\n63:  - task:\r\n70:      revision: 44fa15921b4c889113cc5df03dd4901b49161ab7\r\n95:def _save_model_metadata(model: mteb.Encoder, output_folder: Path) -> None:\r\n96:    meta = model.mteb_model_meta  # type: ignore\r\n98:    revision = meta.revision if meta.revision is not None else \"no_revision_available\"\r\n100:    save_path = output_folder / meta.model_name_as_path() / revision / \"model_meta.json\"\r\n106:def run(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\r\n124:    model = mteb.get_model(args.model, args.model_revision, device=device)\r\n127:        tasks = mteb.get_benchmarks(names=args.benchmarks)\r\n129:        tasks = mteb.get_tasks(\r\n131:  "]
[1660.61743, "o", "          task_types=args.task_types,\r\n133:            tasks=args.tasks,\r\n136:    eval = mteb.MTEB(tasks=tasks)\r\n146:    eval.run(\r\n147:        model,\r\n149:        output_folder=args.output_folder,\r\n157:    _save_model_metadata(model, Path(args.output_folder))\r\n160:def available_benchmarks(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\r\n162:    eval = mteb.MTEB(tasks=benchmarks)\r\n166:def available_tasks(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\r\n167:    tasks = mteb.get_tasks(\r\n169:        task_types=args.task_types,\r\n171:        tasks=args.tasks,\r\n173:    eval = mteb.MTEB(tasks=tasks)\r\n174:    eval.mteb_tasks()\r\n177:def add_benchmark_selection_args(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\r\n189:def add_task_selection_args(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\r\n190:    \"\"\"Adds arguments to the parser for filtering tasks by type, category, language, and task name.\"\"\"\r\n192:        \"--task_types\",\r\n196:        help=\"List of task types (Clustering, Retrieval..) to be evaluated. If None, the filter is not applied\",\r\n203:        "]
[1660.617894, "o", "help=\"List of task categories (s2s, p2p..) to be"]
[1660.61803, "o", " evaluated. If None the filter is not applied\",\r\n207:        \"--tasks\",\r\n211:        help=\"List of tasks to be evaluated. If specified, the other arguments are ignored.\",\r\n223:def add_available_tasks_parser(subparsers) -> None:\r\n225:        \"available_tasks\", help=\"List the available tasks within MTEB\"\r\n227:    add_task_selection_args(parser)\r\n229:    parser.set_defaults(func=available_tasks)\r\n232:def add_available_benchmarks_parser(subparsers) -> None:\r\n241:def add_run_parser(subparsers) -> None:\r\n242:    parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"run\", help=\"Run a model on a set of tasks\")\r\n246:        \"--model\",\r\n248:        help=\"Model to use. Will priotize model implementation in MTEB's model registry, but default to loading the model using sentence-transformers.\",\r\n"]
